  "raw_text": "The stale-error bug was resolved with two complementary fixes that assign clear responsibility for error state. The fused logos runner now authoritatively drops stale per-dimension errors for the eight dimensions it re-tags on a successful pass, clearing the entire error map when only retired dimensions remain. Separately, the completeness predicate was scoped to check only the eight managed dimensions, so a vestigial error from a retired dimension can no longer mark a fully-tagged inference as incomplete. This separates the concern of what dimensions the driver manages from what historical errors may linger in the store.",
